racters at most) at (column p1, row p2) in 1771:2E20's colour", 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:2F37': {'address': '1771:2F37', 'name': 'draw_squad_row', 'purpose': "one row of the squad list: the name (1771:2E93) in 1771:2E20's colour and the position glyph DS:69A8[+6]", 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:2FAD': {'address': '1771:2FAD', 'name': 'player_height', 'purpose': "a player's height, not stored: DS:0E46[+7] + DS:0E54[n mod 12] inches", 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:2FFB': {'address': '1771:2FFB', 'name': 'player_hardness', 'purpose': 'hardness = +5 - (+3 and 1)', 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F007; F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:3041': {'address': '1771:3041', 'name': 'is_two_footed', 'purpose': 'true when +5 + +2 = 30 (the screen then shows "two footed")', 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:3088': {'address': '1771:3088', 'name': 'foot_index', 'purpose': 'returns the foot index DS:0E60[14 * DS:0E7C[n mod 3] + (+7)]; the player screen shows the word DS:0F2C + 6 * index', 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:30D9': {'address': '1771:30D9', 'name': 'player_leadership', 'purpose': 'leadership v = ((+3) - (+5)) mod 8, halved when +1 < 0x15', 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F008; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:3216': {'address': '1771:3216', 'name': 'player_unavailable', 'purpose': 'returns 0 only when player +0x0E > 0 and bits 8, 6 and 3 of +0x10 are clear, else 1; 377E then gives strength 0 and D733 rerolls a scorer', 'confidence': 'likely', 'basis': 'read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c; read decompiled/seg_0791_08.c'}, '1771:3291': {'address': '1771:3291', 'name': 'roll_peak_age', 'purpose': 'draws +2: DS:0E80[gk] + b - a with a then b = rand(3)', 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F007; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:32EB': {'address': '1771:32EB', 'name': 'compute_ability', 'purpose': 'computes +4 from +1, +2, +3: +3 inside the copy branch +2..+2+3; below it k = (+2 - +1) div 2 (SIGNED idiv; k = 0 at +2-1, so the maximum spans five ages), above it k = +1 - (+2+3); +4 = AL, the low byte of ((+3 * (0x10 - k)) mod 65536) div 16, with the factor a wrapping 16-bit word (k > 16)', 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F007; F009; F016; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c; read code/seg_1771_05.asm'}, '1771:33CD': {'address': '1771:33CD', 'name': 'force_tactic4_off', 'purpose': "sets set element 8 (bit 7, the override of tactic 4) and clears element 4 (bit 3) of the player's +0x0F, unconditionally - the override of tackling to avoid injury; 1771:3431 calls it first when the player's hardness is below 4", 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F007; F010; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:3431': {'address': '1771:3431', 'name': 'set_player_tactics', 'purpose': "sets the player's +0x0F tactic bits (Pascal set, 214B:0C79 / 0CA1) from the player's own fields, never from a byte of the country record: when the hardness (1771:2FFB) is below 4 it calls 1771:33CD first (the override of tackling to avoid injury); for positions 0, 1, 3 and 4 (goalkeeper, sweeper, left and right back; the set 0x1B tested at 1771:3411) it sets element 5, then element 1 (push forward, or leave box for a goalkeeper); for position 2 (centre back) it sets element 5 when +5 < 14, then always element 6 and element 2 (the quick-pass override; element 1 stays clear, so that override is stay back); it only sets bits (33CD clears element 4), so callers that want a fresh derivation clear +0xF first (0791:BC5D, 1771:34E7, 0791:C5DC; 0791:BBFF does not)", 'confidence': 'established', 'basis': 'F007; F010; read decompiled/seg_1771_02.c'}, '1771:34E7': {'address': '1771:34E7', 'name': 'reset_own_tactics', 'purpose': "clears +0xF (own_tactic_set) of a country's players and re-deri